{"metrics":{"latencyMs":3272},"output":{"message":{"content":[{"reasoningContent":{"reasoningText":{"text":"The user asks: \"Think step by step: What is 17 * 23? Show your reasoning process.\" So we need to compute 17 * 23. But the user explicitly wants step by step reasoning, perhaps by expansion: (17 * 20) + (17 * 3) = 340 + 51 = 391. Or using algorithm / decomposition. We can show detailed reasoning: Write 17 * 23 = (10+7)*(20+3) = 10*20 + 10*3 + 7*20 + 7*3 = 200 + 30 + 140 + 21 = 391. Or 23*17 = 23*10 + 23*7 = 230 + 161 = 391. Provide explanation.\n\nWe then show step-by-step in plain text. We'll also mention perhaps cross-check: 17 * 23 = 391. So we should deliver final answer: 391. Also show the steps.\n\nThus the best answer: \"17×23 = (17×20)+(17×3) = 340+51 = 391.\" Provide full reasoning.\n\nWe can note that 17x23 = (20+3)*(10+7)... etc. Provide answer.\n\nOk finalize."}}},{"text":"Sure! Let’s break the multiplication down into simpler pieces so you can see exactly how we get the answer.\n\n### 1. Use the distributive property\nWe can write each number as a sum of simpler numbers:\n\n- \\(17 = 10 + 7\\)\n- \\(23 = 20 + 3\\)\n\nNow multiply \\((10 + 7)\\) by \\((20 + 3)\\):\n\n\\[\n(10 + 7)(20 + 3)\n\\]\n\n### 2. Expand the product\nApply the distributive law (multiplying each part of the first parenthesis by each part of the second):\n\n\\[\n= 10 \\times 20 \\;+\\; 10 \\times 3 \\;+\\; 7 \\times 20 \\;+\\; 7 \\times 3\n\\]\n\n### 3. Compute each small product\n- \\(10 \\times 20 = 200\\)\n- \\(10 \\times 3 = 30\\)\n- \\(7 \\times 20 = 140\\)\n- \\(7 \\times 3 = 21\\)\n\n### 4. Add the results together\n\\[\n200 \\;+\\; 30 \\;+\\; 140 \\;+\\; 21 = 200 + 30 = 230,\\;\n230 + 140 = 370,\\;\n370 + 21 = 391\n\\]\n\n### 5. Final answer\n\\[\n17 \\times 23 = 391\n\\]\n\n---\n\nYou can also check quickly by using the “split and add” trick:\n\n- \\(23 \\times 17 = 23 \\times (10 + 7) = 23 \\times 10 + 23 \\times 7\\)\n- \\(23 \\times 10 = 230\\)\n- \\(23 \\times 7 = 161\\)\n- Sum: \\(230 + 161 = 391\\)\n\nEither way, the result is **391**."}],"role":"assistant"}},"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"inputTokens":85,"outputTokens":678,"serverToolUsage":{},"totalTokens":763}}539 2852
